{"availability":"available","full":"nsubordin81/blog.synapseflux.com","name":"blog.synapseflux.com","description":"blog space for synapseflux site, based on blog-in-a-box repository https://github.com/excellalabs/blog-in-a-box","category":"Other","language":"Shell","stars":2,"forks":1,"created":"2023-03-16T21:00:10Z","updated":"2026-05-12T23:31:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://bloginaboxdemo.com/2022/01/netlify-preview/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T21:32:08.073Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T21:32:08.073Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T21:32:08.073Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T23:20:11.680Z","stars":2,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-16T21:32:08.073Z","stars":2,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A quick, all in one stop for someone to get a blog presence up and running.","GitHub Pages, where we presume you are deploying, has some rules for what can be deployed. If deploying from the main branch, you have two options: (root), or the base directory of the repository, and /docs. In our case, we didn't want the other stuff in the root to get confused with the actual blog stuff, so we chose /docs because that's the name available that fits into our batteries-included setup with the least amount of fuss.","There are ways to customize this, particularly by using a gh-pages branch and creating a GitHub Action to push to it, but we figured that might be over-complicated. Feel free to reach out if you want to set that up and we may follow up with some more on this in the future."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nsubordin81/blog.synapseflux.com/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a488a9ed82831c6dde1369acca4c1c7b7a1dbcde514c25e2390c40b7d4a28b4f","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:11.766Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:11.766Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A quick, all in one stop for someone to get a blog pres